    title: "“If you played this card using [union]” (#930, BT5-037 front 10, BT6-036 front 10)",
    body: "22-13 and 3-1-4, owner's ruling of 25 Oct 2026. “Then shuffle your deck, and **if you played this card using [union]**, draw 1 card” (BT5-037) and “When you play this card, draw 1 card, and **if this card was played using [union]**, draw 1 more card” (BT6-036) are one condition, `playedUsing(sel: [self], what: Union)`: did this copy enter by a [Union-(type)] skill's own play? **Only a successful entry counts**: the copy remembers it (`VmCard.enteredUsing`) only when `resolvePlay` lands it, so a play a [Counter: Play] placed in the Drop or returned to the hand instead, or one that failed to enter (22-13-4-5-1, 22-13-5-4-2, 22-13-6-3-2), is not one — and the returned copy, played ordinarily afterwards, does not inherit it. The memory is the copy's for as long as it stays, across turns, and goes with any change of area. BT5-037 places itself in the Drop as its cost before the effect, so “this card” is read as it was when the skill was activated (`ScriptFrame.selfEnteredUsing`); an [Auto] reads it as it was when the Auto was triggered (`VmPending.selfEnteredUsing`), so BT6-036 played by [Union-Potara] and KO'd by a [Counter: Play] before its on-play [Auto] resolves still draws the extra card — the condition is about how it was played (owner's ruling, 25 Oct 2026); a later ordinary play's Autos never carry an earlier entry. Only bare “[union]” is read in this condition; a named variant is read only as the gate of a trigger (next entry). Two shared readings came with it: “draw 1 **more** card” is a draw (also EX06-27), and “choose **up to 1 each of** blue {A} and {B} cards with energy costs of 2 from your deck and add them to your hand” is one “up to 1” choice per name, the colour before the first name and an energy-cost or power measure after the last applying to every name — a **labelled best guess** (also BT2-016 front 0, BT4-034 front 10). The [Auto] triggers “when this card is played using [Union]” / “with [union]” / “by a [union] skill” (BT14-114, BT5-039, BT28-097 …) are the next entry. Proof: `scripts/verify/played-via-union-930.ts`.",
