    body: "22-13 and 9-6-2, owner's rulings of 25 Oct 2026. “[Auto] **When this card is played using [Union]**, draw 1 card” (BT14-114), “When **you play this card with [union]**, …” (BT5-039, BT2-085, BT7-123, P-109), “When you play this card **using [union]**, …” (BT4-108) and “When this card is played **by a [union] skill**, …” (BT28-097, BT28-099) are the moment `played` with a gate on it: the record's condition is `playedUsing(sel: [self], what: Union)`, and a named variant (“using [Union-Potara]”) is `what: Union-Potara` — that [Union] keyword only. Read as a plain `played` before, they fired on an ordinary play too. The gate is a **trigger condition**, not a check at resolution: `resolvePlay` withdraws the Auto from any play that is not a **successful** entry by the named [Union] keyword's own play — an ordinary play, a play a [Counter: Play] placed in the Drop or returned to the hand instead, one that failed to enter, or one by another variant — so it is never pending, never ordered and uses no [Once per turn] (`vm/triggers.ts` `unionPlayGate`, read off the record: a lone IF, or a chain of lone IFs behind a price's condition). A card played by **another card's** [Union-Absorb] counts (owner's ruling). The Autos that entry pended carry it (`VmPending.selfEnteredUsing`), so a copy KO'd before its Auto resolves still resolves it: it entered via [Union] (owner's ruling). Only the card's own play, and only the whole moment: “When **your** <Gogeta> card is played by a [union] skill” (BT22-033, BT25-036 back, P-682) is the next entry, and “…played using [union-potara] **or attacks**” (BT4-019 front 30) — a gate on one half only — stays unread. BT6-036's “…and if this card was played using [union], draw 1 more card” is a condition later in the effect, not a gate: that Auto answers every play. Proof: `scripts/verify/union-play-triggers-930.ts`.",
